{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg8pzqAcy9z8aHfLYKXfe","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_017Et6WmPNa363xxpDZidz6J","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/nick/code/webtorrent-desktop.memory-leaks-03-server-holds-counted-on-request; python3 - <<'EOF'\np='src/engine/AGENTS.md'\ns=open(p).read()\nold='''Poster generation and playback can\nhold servers for different torrents at once, so a single module-level\n`server` is not enough any more.\n'''\nnew='''Poster generation and playback can\nhold servers for different torrents at once, so a single module-level\n`server` is not enough any more.\n\nA hold is counted the moment `wt-start-server` arrives, not on\n`ready`: the entry (`{ torrent, holders, server, info }`) exists from\nthe first request, `server` stays null until the torrent is ready and\n`info` until it is listening. Only the first early request parks a\nready handler, and that handler (and the `listen` callback) does\nnothing once `servers.get(infoHash)` is no longer its entry. So a\n`wt-stop-server` is honoured in any state and the last one always\nwins. `forgetServer` is the one way an entry goes: the last release,\n`stopAllServers` and the torrent's `close` all call it, and\n`destroyServer` also splices the server out of WebTorrent's private\n`torrent._servers`, which otherwise only empties on destroy.\n\n`test/unit/engine-entry.js` checks this on the real sidecar by probing\nthe reported port with `net.connect`. Its `withEngine` helper spawns\nand connects; reuse it for new sidecar cases. A `.torrent` path is\nparsed asynchronously, so a `wt-start-server` in the same burst as\n`wt-start-torrenting` finds no torrent -- wait for `wt-parsed` first.\nMissing files verify in milliseconds, so a test that needs to act\nbefore `ready` writes full-length sparse files of zeros into the\ndownload directory to widen the window.\n'''\nassert old in s\ns=s.replace(old,new,1)\nold2='''`test/unit/engine-torrent-close-wiring.js` pins this by source scan.'''\nnew2='''The streaming server entry is forgotten there too (`forgetServer`).\n\n`test/unit/engine-torrent-close-wiring.js` pins this by source scan.'''\ns=s.replace(old2,new2,1)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\nmkdir -p .nightralph; cat > .nightralph/notes.md <<'EOF'\n# Ticket 03: server holds counted on request, forgotten on close\n\n## Implemented\n- `src/engine/index.js`: `startServer` creates the entry\n  `{ torrent, holders, server: null, info: null }` on arrival and counts\n  the hold at once; the first early request parks one ready handler\n  (`listenForEntry`). `listenForEntry` and the `listen` callback bail if\n  `servers.get(infoHash) !== entry`. `stopServer` decrements in any\n  state and calls `forgetServer` at zero. `forgetServer` deletes the\n  entry and `destroyServer`s (splices from `torrent._servers`, then\n  `server.destroy()`). `stopAllServers` and `torrentClose` (after the\n  duplicate guard) call `forgetServer`. Unknown torrent: still no hold,\n  no reply.\n- `test/unit/engine-entry.js`: four real-sidecar tests plus helpers\n  `withEngine`, `startServer`, `accepts` (net.connect probe),\n  `waitForPort`, `delay`.\n- `test/unit/engine-torrent-close-wiring.js`: scan that torrentClose\n  calls `forgetServer(infoHash)` after the guard, and that forgetServer\n  deletes and destroys.\n- `src/engine/AGENTS.md`: server lifecycle + sidecar test gotchas.\n\n## How ACs were read\n- Burst test: a .torrent path parses asynchronously, so start-server in\n  the same burst as start-torrenting finds no torrent (passes trivially).\n  The test waits for `wt-parsed`, then sends start+stop in one burst and\n  asserts ready had not yet arrived. Missing files verified too fast\n  (ready beat the burst), so per the ticket the fixture got more to\n  verify: a full-length sparse file of zeros in the download dir. Stable\n  over 5 runs; failed on old code for the right reason.\n- Two starts / two stops and two starts / one stop run after ready (they\n  need the reply's URL). Pre-ready counting is covered by the burst test.\n- Removing from `torrent._servers` is not automated (spec says so).\n- Items 1-4 share one engine change and one commit; item 5 (scan) is a\n  second commit.\nEOF\ngit add src/engine/AGENTS.md test/unit/engine-torrent-close-wiring.js && git commit -q -m \"test: pin that a torrent's close forgets its server entry\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\" && git log --oneline -1"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":352,"cache_read_input_tokens":92635,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":352},"output_tokens":232,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"51376cad-72e5-4753-a12b-f4c0880ced8a","uuid":"243447bf-a561-416b-8ff7-e8f7a666a166","timestamp":"2026-10-18T01:23:44.557Z","request_id":"req_011Cg8pzptkhobdFVSNE5hMP","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_017Et6WmPNa363xxpDZidz6J":{"command":"cd /Users/nick/code/webtorrent-desktop.memory-leaks-03-server-holds-counted-on-request; python3 - <<'EOF'\np='src/engine/AGENTS.md'\ns=open(p).read()\nold='''Poster generation and playback can\nhold servers for different torrents at once, so a single module-level\n`server` is not enough any more.\n'''\nnew='''Poster generation and playback can\nhold servers for different torrents at once, so a single module-level\n`server` is not enough any more.\n\nA hold is counted the moment `wt-start-server` arrives, not on\n`ready`: the entry (`{ torrent, holders, server, info }`) exists from\nthe first request, `server` stays null until the torrent is ready and\n`info` until it is listening. Only the first early request parks a\nready handler, and that handler (and